      "evidence": "scripts/rollout_project.py migrate_ci_runner_answers: `answers.get(\"scm_provider\", \"github\") != \"github\"`. The user's no-fallback rule asks for a loud failure on missing required input, or an explicit decision to keep this default.",
      "id": "rollout-scm-provider-implicit-default",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The preflight silently treats a missing scm_provider answer as github, which is a default that masks a missing input. It is the same as Copier's own default, but the code doesn't say so or fail on a missing answer."
    },
    {
      "evidence": "platform_doctor_module() loads PLATFORM_ROOT/template/scripts/platform_doctor.py. The design says the rollout must not record answers the doctor would reject, but the target tag's doctor is never consulted. The parity test only covers the current checkout.",
      "id": "rollout-doctor-rule-from-platform-checkout",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The label rule and runs-on regexes come from the doctor in the rollout tool's own PLATFORM_ROOT checkout, not from the doctor shipped in the target release. If the two diverge, the rollout could record answers the target's doctor rejects."
    }
